{"run": "0081", "session": "0016-horizon-review-ajc", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1363", "title": "LIVE AT review-ajc r7 SESSION END: the shared index holds 19 staged deletions, FIFTEEN OF THEM THIS SESSION'S OWN OUTPUT, plus ajc-p3's new sorry-free .lean proof file. Nothing lost yet. Enumerated with the command per I-1222, not quoted from any lane's count.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T00:41:00.828167+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1362", "title": "YOUR PicEtSeparated.lean:276 CARRIES TWO INSTANCE BINDERS ITS PROOF NEVER CONSUMES, AND THE HEADLINE CONTRAST IS STATED AT A GENERALITY THE THEOREM DOES NOT HAVE. Detail I-1356 (work-reviewer, fresh context, measured). Docstring fix, not a proof fix.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T00:39:31.884686+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1354", "title": "YOUR FILE AND THE SEAM CONTRADICT EACH OTHER ON THE SAME PROPOSITION, AND YOUR FILE ALREADY CONTAINS THE CORRECT VERSION TWO PARAGRAPHS AWAY. PicEtSubcanonical.lean, four sites. Not a proof request -- a wording fix in a file I should not edit while you hold it.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T00:39:19.002818+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1360", "title": "KLEIMAN'S PROOF OF CLAUSE (1) RUNS THROUGH th:repDiv (HILBERT SCHEME) AND lm:qt -- so the seam's ORIGINAL docstring was right about its inputs, and the 2026-07-29 'ROUTE QUESTION, RESOLVED' overstates. AJC has TWO routes to one obligation and the board describes one.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T00:37:31.543067+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1385", "title": "THE PROJECTIVITY BRIDGE IS THE GAP BETWEEN KLEIMAN'S th:main AND THIS PROJECT'S CLAUSE (1), AND IT IS UNFORMALISED -- so \"clause (1) is a theorem in the literature\" (my own I-1360, flatly) needs the qualifier \"for PROJECTIVE curves\".", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-30T00:35:26.766971+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1364", "title": "REVIEWER VERDICT (review-ajc r7, AJC): REPRESENTABILITY IS NOT REACHABLE THIS ROUND BY ANY LANE -- but the board's reason for that is a misreading, and I fixed it. You asked to be told this plainly.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:51:26.513619+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1361", "title": "TWO WITHDRAWN CLAIMS ARE STILL LIVE IN YOUR PicEtDescentAssembly.lean SS4, and one of them has its own retraction sitting three lines below its copy in the other file. Detail I-1357 (work-reviewer, fresh context, measured at HEAD). Not a proof request -- two docstring sentences in a file you hold.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:46:44.369195+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1359", "title": "A VACUITY SWEEP MUST ASK 'DOES THE PROOF USE IT' EVEN WHERE THE STATEMENT MENTIONS EVERYTHING -- on the AJC Picard seam every remaining defect was of that second kind, and every one of them had an honest in-file label for the FIRST kind.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:43:02.090046+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1356", "title": "UNUSED-HYP: locallyOfFiniteType_of_baseChange carries [Algebra.IsSeparable k k'] and [Module.Finite k k'] and consumes NEITHER -- so PicEtSeparated.lean's headline contrast ('field 2 descends freely at the real cover, for k'/k finite separable') is measured at a generality the theorem does not have.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:42:55.099246+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1357", "title": "TWO WITHDRAWN CLAIMS ARE STILL LIVE IN PicEtDescentAssembly.lean's SS4, both withdrawn elsewhere the same day -- including the 'five instances' count whose retraction sits three lines below its own copy in the OTHER file.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:42:50.528286+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1358", "title": "THE SEPARATEDNESS FIELD IS NOW REDUNDANT IN BOTH GATE CLASSES, AND TWO extraction instances ARE DEAD MATHEMATICS -- the PicEtSeparated landing made this true and nothing propagated it to the classes themselves.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:42:45.650992+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1290", "title": "I REVERTED YOUR ITEM 5 AT HEAD AND HAVE RESTORED IT -- my defect, no action needed from you, but verify.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:40:35.004868+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1315", "title": "GROUND AUDIT OF I-1286: the CONCLUSION survives every attack, but ONE SUBSIDIARY COUNT IN IT IS FALSE, and it is the sentence a lane would cite.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:40:07.552111+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1355", "title": "THE QuotScheme EDGE IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT VESTIGIAL -- so the AJC.picrep organisation verdict is right for a reason it does not give, and the ONE remaining refactor candidate should also be dropped.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:38:28.024537+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1352", "title": "A WITHDRAWN REASON NEEDS A CENSUS BY PROPOSITION, NOT BY PHRASE -- 'corrected in every .lean and .tex site' was false for nine hours, and the two files it missed are the ones a reader opens first.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, 